# perp-lab core

Reproducible framework for discovering/validating interpretable intraday
strategies on BTC/ETH USDT-M perpetual futures (Master's Thesis).

## Current scope: Phase 1 (data + EDA)

In scope: environment, data contract, acquisition, quality validation, reusable
EDA. Do NOT create strategy, search, backtesting, regime-model, meta-labeling,
MLflow, API or frontend modules yet. See `docs/roadmap.md`.

## Architecture

- Library code lives in `src/perp_lab/{config,data,validation,eda,utils}` and is
  typed and unit-tested.
- Configuration is data in `configs/*.yaml`, validated by pydantic models.
- Notebooks (later) only narrate; they must call library functions, not hold
  reusable logic.
- Timestamps are tz-aware UTC; bars are labeled by open time, left-closed.

## Commands

```bash
uv sync --extra dev
uv run ruff check . && uv run ruff format --check .
uv run pyright
uv run pytest -m "not network"
```

## Dependencies

Add dependencies with `uv add` (or `uv add --dev`). Never hand-edit version
pins. Keep Phase-1 dependencies free of strategy/ML/web packages.
